description: Test evidence, tenant isolation, and coverage honesty
globs: tests/**
alwaysApply: false
---

# Testing

- Write the failing characterization of an invariant before the implementation when the behavior is domain-critical.
- Do not add assertions that only exist to satisfy coverage.
- Do not change a correct test to make an incorrect implementation pass.
- Tenant isolation tests must show Tenant A cannot read Tenant B.
- Coverage numbers come from the tool. If the tool is absent, report NOT APPLICABLE. Never invent a percentage.
- Domain, contracts, authz, and CRS helpers target at least 95 percent line, branch, and function coverage once the tool exists.
